<title>FRANCE: Elf wants to buy back up to 15 pct shares.</title>
<headline>Elf wants to buy back up to 15 pct shares.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Elf Aquitaine confirmed on Thursday that it would ask its shareholders for an authorisation to buy back up to 15 percent of its share capital.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman said it would seek a five-year authorisation for the share repurchases.</p>
<p>Earlier, a spokesman had confirmed a media report that the oil group intended to seek approval for buy-backs at a May 30 shareholder meeting, but said this did not automatically mean Elf was going to carry out repurchases.</p>
<p>Elf shares were trading at 560, up 0.9 percent, at 1146 GMT.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
